      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "We assume that John Mark wrote it, and I won't take away from the evidence of that, but I want to claim Peter as the author of it. This is Peter's account of Jesus' ministry. Matthew's account is all about what Jesus said. We will see that Mark's account is all about what Jesus did. We can see throughout the book of Acts that Mark was Peter's right-hand man. His \"son in the faith,\" if you will. It seems that all of the Apostles had at least one man that would help serve the ministry with them, and Mark happened to be that man.",
