  "mark_1_4": [
    {
      "id": "mark_1_4_mark-1-1-8_22",
      "book": "Mark",
      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 4,
      "startVerse": 4,
      "endVerse": 4,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "He preaches a message about repentance and baptism. Baptism is not a salvation tactic (I think we should understand that very clearly right off the bat). We do not get baptized to be saved. That has never been a method of salvation (and we will look into that deeper as we go along, especially in Acts). He preached about baptism because he is \"preparing the way\" for something better than his water baptism. Baptism was a symbol of what was to come. Christ would bring something better.",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "kind": "comment",
      "quoteStyle": null,
      "sectionId": "mark-1-1-8",
      "sectionTitle": "John The Baptizer",
      "isIntroduction": false,
      "verseLabel": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "mark_1_4_mark-1-1-8_23",
      "book": "Mark",
      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 4,
      "startVerse": 4,
      "endVerse": 4,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "Repentance is the thing that hangs people up, however. Baptism is one topic saved throughout multiple facets of scripture (you can jump to the letters from Peter if you want to get a quick note on this), but repentance is something that must be established right here in this chapter of scripture in order for us to get a clear view of it. \"Repentance\" means \"a change of mind, as it appears to one who repents, of a purpose he has formed or of something he has done.” There are people who say that \"repentance is a work.” Repentance is not a work if it's simply just \"changing your mind\" according to Strong's Concordance. It's simply saying, \"You know what, I'm wrong, and I want to accept what is right.” However, there is a continual repentance after salvation.",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "kind": "comment",
      "quoteStyle": null,
      "sectionId": "mark-1-1-8",
      "sectionTitle": "John The Baptizer",
      "isIntroduction": false,
      "verseLabel": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "mark_1_4_mark-1-1-8_24",
      "book": "Mark",
      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 4,
      "startVerse": 4,
      "endVerse": 4,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "The best way I can describe repentance is in a twofold manner. The first is through salvation. In order for someone to be saved, they have to be willing to change their mind about their sin. They are certainly FOR their sin before Christ, but when they come to Christ they have a choice to make. Do they reject Him and continue their life of sin, or do they accept Him and repent from it? That is what I refer to as \"initial repentance.” That is the start of their salvation.",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "kind": "comment",
      "quoteStyle": null,
      "sectionId": "mark-1-1-8",
      "sectionTitle": "John The Baptizer",
      "isIntroduction": false,
      "verseLabel": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "mark_1_4_mark-1-1-8_25",
      "book": "Mark",
      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 4,
      "startVerse": 4,
      "endVerse": 4,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "After they take that step forward, they are then in a mode of what I call \"continual repentance.” They will be changing their minds and attitudes about literally everything they thought was good before if it rejects the Lord's grace and glory. That is the message that John is preaching, and he's preaching it because that is the lifestyle that one must live if they are going to genuinely follow the Lord in faith and believing. We cannot just have faith. We must actually FOLLOW God. We cannot follow Him without a repentant Spirit. Faith and repentance walk hand-in-hand. The book of James is full of representations of this.",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "kind": "comment",
      "quoteStyle": null,
      "sectionId": "mark-1-1-8",
      "sectionTitle": "John The Baptizer",
      "isIntroduction": false,
      "verseLabel": "4"
    }
  ],
