          "verse": 0,
          "startVerse": 0,
          "endVerse": 0,
          "author": "Tried By Fire",
          "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
          "text": "Most people believe this gospel was written by John Mark, a man that was not an eyewitness to Christ, but became a disciple of Christ through the preaching and teaching of the first-century church (specifically through Peter and Paul's preaching, which can be further expounded in the book of Acts). This is the oldest gospel account written, and it is said to have been purposefully written to account for the facts of Jesus' true ministry. Apparently, Peter had been preaching a storm to some first-time hearers, and these people enjoyed his sermon and testimony so much that they asked for it in writing. That is where some of the questions come in.",
          "likes": 0,
          "isLikedByUser": false,
          "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
          "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
          "kind": "comment",
          "quoteStyle": null,
          "sectionId": "mark-1-intro",
